      <p>Let Claude search Indeed for you every day or week and check each internship against the GJU rules. Then load the results here to filter them, read why each one does or does not fit, and mark the ones you applied to.</p>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><b>Connect Indeed to Claude.</b> In Claude, open Settings → Connectors and add Indeed.</li>
        <li><b>Schedule the search in Claude Cowork.</b> In a Cowork task, type <code>/schedule</code>, choose daily or weekly, and paste this with your major and city filled in:
          <div class="prompt-box">
            <p id="results-prompt">Find German Year internships on Indeed for me and check each one against the GJU rules.
My major: [your GJU major, for example Computer Engineering]
Where: [a city, or anywhere in Germany]
Follow https://hamza928505.github.io/GJUYearKit/.claude/skills/gju-internships/SKILL.md exactly, and finish with its step 5: save the results as gju-internships-YYYY-MM-DD.json.</p>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm" id="results-copy-prompt"><i class="fa-solid fa-copy" aria-hidden="true"></i>Copy</button>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li><b>Download the file.</b> Each run saves a file named gju-internships-<i>date</i>.json. Open the run in Claude and download it.</li>
        <li><b>Load it here.</b> Choose the file, or drop it on this box. It stays in this browser: nothing is uploaded.
          <div class="hero-cta"><button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="results-choose"><i class="fa-solid fa-folder-open" aria-hidden="true"></i>Choose file</button></div>
